From 3d8b7cfde9d1db0e2a288afce111cbf202d42a66 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sabith Saheb <shabi7204192361@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 17:42:48 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] ecx_kmgmt: free the private key with the secure heap aware
 free

ecx_set_params() discards the private key when a new encoded public
key is set through OSSL_PKEY_PARAM_ENCODED_PUBLIC_KEY, which is what
EVP_PKEY_set1_encoded_public_key() uses for provided keys. It released
the key with OPENSSL_clear_free(), but ossl_ecx_key_allocate_privkey()
allocates the private key of generated and derived ECX keys with
OPENSSL_secure_zalloc(). When the application has enabled the secure
heap with CRYPTO_secure_malloc_init(), the pointer lives in the locked
arena and OPENSSL_clear_free() hands it to the system free(). ASan
reports a bad-free in ecx_set_params and the arena allocation is never
returned, so CRYPTO_secure_malloc_done() can no longer release the heap.

Use OPENSSL_secure_clear_free() like every other release of an ECX
private key (ossl_ecx_key_free, ossl_ecx_key_fromdata). It falls back to
the normal free for keys that were imported with OPENSSL_malloc().

Fixes: 6a9bd9298bd7 "Make EVP_PKEY_[get1|set1]_tls_encodedpoint work with provided keys"
Assisted-by: Claude Code:claude-fable-5-1
Reviewed-by: Eugene Syromiatnikov <esyr@openssl.org>
Reviewed-by: Nikola Pajkovsky <nikolap@openssl.org>
Merge-date: Fri Oct 30 03:45:12 2026
Merged-from: https://github.com/openssl/openssl/pull/33360
(cherry picked from commit f3e3dd00b01856659d57d15991b4994419c63893)
---
 providers/implementations/keymgmt/ecx_kmgmt.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/providers/implementations/keymgmt/ecx_kmgmt.c b/providers/implementations/keymgmt/ecx_kmgmt.c
index a12b02e..eb075ef 100644
--- a/providers/implementations/keymgmt/ecx_kmgmt.c
+++ b/providers/implementations/keymgmt/ecx_kmgmt.c
@@ -449,7 +449,7 @@ static int ecx_set_params(void *key, const OSSL_PARAM params[])
             || !OSSL_PARAM_get_octet_string(p.pub, &buf, sizeof(ecxkey->pubkey),
                 NULL))
             return 0;
-        OPENSSL_clear_free(ecxkey->privkey, ecxkey->keylen);
+        OPENSSL_secure_clear_free(ecxkey->privkey, ecxkey->keylen);
         ecxkey->privkey = NULL;
         ecxkey->haspubkey = 1;
     }
